    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d264-a11">

                <pb facs="0275" n="953" sameAs="frus:frus1863p2/pg953"/>


                <head>Mr. Burlingame to Prince
                        Kung</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States</hi>,
                                <hi rendition="#italic">Peking</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-06-19"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >June</hi> 19, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>I hasten to acknowledge the receipt of your Imperial Highness’s despatch of
                    yesterday’s date, and to express my satisfaction at the manner in which you have
                    settled the question in dispute between us. It is by acting thus, in a spirit of
                    fairness and justice, that the amicable relations between our two countries are
                    to be strengthened and perpetual peace maintained.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <p>ANSON BURLINGAME.</p>
                <p>
                    <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Prince Kung</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Secretary in Chief for Foreign Affairs.</hi></placeName></p>
            </div>
        </body>
